    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-81887705-a298-47fd-8152-f42c5fc0bf97": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL 497467 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Dentistry Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL Employee Type: Faculty Department: COMPREHNSV DENTISTRY & BIOMATL Campus Location: COMPREHENSIVE DENT AND BIOMATE Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health – New Orleans School of Dentistry is seeking applicants for a full time, non-tenure track position to instruct and mentor dental students in Operative Dentistry. Primary responsibilities will involve providing clinical supervision, competency assessment and constructive feedback in both Simulation lab and Clinic. Secondary responsibilities include some teaching of pre-clinical students, lecturing, and administrative duties. Must have 10 years of clinical experience and be eligible to practice dentistry in Louisiana. The candidate must have a DDS/DMD degree in General Dentistry. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: DDS/DMD Other Education if applicable: Doctor of Dental Medicine or Doctor of Dental Surgery Required Field of Study: General Dentistry Certifications or Licenses Required: Louisiana State Board of Dentistry and Louisiana Driver’s license; BLS certification for Healthcare Number of years required to perform the job: 10 years as a licensed Dentist in good standing Type of experience required to perform the job: At least 10 years in academia or in General Dentist office Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits off