      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, LARYNGOLOGY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, LARYNGOLOGY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, LARYNGOLOGY 497453 Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, LARYNGOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Otolaryngology Head & Neck Surgery Campus Location: OTORHINOLARYNGOLOGY/FACULTY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Otolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery of LSU Health Sciences Center is actively seeking a candidate for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) fellowship trained in Laryngology to practice in Baton Rouge, LA. This is an excellent opportunity to join our growing practice. Responsibilities include patient care, resident and medical student education, and the pursuit of clinical research. Extensive collaborative research opportunities are available. Our faculty team members enjoy liberal cross-coverage for weekend and holiday on-call responsibilities and share the benefit of subspecialty support in otology, rhinology, head and neck oncology, pediatric otolaryngology, and plastic/reconstructive surgery. Salary and rank will be commensurate with the knowledge, education and experience of the individual. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Fellowship trained in Laryngology Certifications or Licenses Required: BC/BE (or equivalent) in Otolaryngology; Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before date of hire. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligibl