    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-radiology-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-24efcdea-c2de-4735-a8fa-77415a905ab5": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, RADIOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, RADIOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, RADIOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, RADIOLOGY 497458 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, RADIOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Radiology Campus Location: RADIOLOGY/FACULTY/NEW ORLEANS/ Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Radiology at the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) School of Medicine in New Orleans is seeking candidates for an academic faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) with expertise in Pediatric Interventional Radiology. Our department is dedicated to excellence in patient care, education, and scholarly activity. Responsibilities will include all aspects of Interventional Radiology – procedures, outpatient clinical care and inpatient clinical care. Call will include weeknights, weekends and holidays, with ample time off. This is a wonderful opportunity for an Interventionalist to practice cutting edge Interventional Radiology in a stimulating environment Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Interventional Radiology Fellowship or IR-DR Residency Certifications or Licenses Required: BR certified in IR/DR or on the pathway to full-board certification; licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts;