    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/instructor-assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-instruction-revised-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "INSTRUCTOR/ ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - INSTRUCTION (REVISED)",
      "description": "INSTRUCTOR/ ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - INSTRUCTION (REVISED) - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States INSTRUCTOR/ ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - INSTRUCTION (REVISED) - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! INSTRUCTOR/ ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - INSTRUCTION (REVISED) 497071 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: INSTRUCTOR/ ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - INSTRUCTION Employee Type: Faculty Department: LSUNO Anatomy Campus Location: ANATOMY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Cell Biology and Anatomy at the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center School of Medicine in New Orleans is seeking a candidate for an academic faculty position at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor on the Instruction (non-tenure) track. This individual will contribute to the departmental mission in a team-teaching oriented environment. The successful candidate will have the ability to immediately instruct in Gross Anatomy. Candidates with experience in cadaveric dissection in a health science center environment will be given prioritized consideration. Expertise in one or more of the following fields is preferred but not required: neuroanatomy, embryology and histology. Applicants must have completed the requirements for a PhD, MD, or DPT by the hire date at the Assistant Professor level, and for higher ranks they should have teaching experience commensurate with the desired rank. Teaching duties may be assigned within the multiple health professional schools of the LSU Health Sciences Center (Medicine, Dentistry, Allied Health and Nursing). We are looking for dedicated educators, participation in educational research is preferred but not required. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or MD Required Field of Study: Anatomy or a related field Substitution: DPT or equivalent can substitute for PhD or MD. Master's degree in appropriate field may substitute for appointment at the rank of Instructor. Special Instructions Summary Qualified applicants must submit a current curriculum vitae, a combined teaching/research statement, and contact information for three professional references. Please include the teaching/research statement and references with the curriculum vitae in a single attachment. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 25d74d31 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUNO Anatomy (NO11010) LSUNO Anatomy (NO11010) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) cd4563a6 Last Name (required) dccb9d25 Email (required) e002994f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 70f05fc6 Last Name (required) 7daaed21 Email (required) 580a6f9c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
