    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-14efc980-388f-41c7-a7c8-776a1121aba9": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR 497424 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Allied Health Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: LSUNO Communication Disorders Campus Location: COMMUNICATION DISORDERS Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Communication Disorders in the School of Allied Health Professions at the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center in New Orleans seeks candidates for an open rank Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Communication Disorders (Audiology). The successful candidate will be responsible for courses in the Doctor of Audiology curriculum, with potential teaching assignments in hearing aids and electrophysiology. Clinical experience in vestibular assessment and management is required. Additional responsibilities include providing direct patient care and student supervision in the clinic, mentoring students, and service to the department, school, and university. The successful candidate will demonstrate effectiveness in teaching, scholarship, and service, demonstrate effective communication skills, and demonstrate a commitment to collegiality in the workplace. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Doctorate Required Field of Study: Communication Sciences or related field Certifications or Licenses Required: Certificate of Clinical Competence in Audiology from ASHA, Louisiana license in audiology or eligibility for licensure Number of years required to perform the job: 1 Type of experience required to perform the job: At least 1 year of clinical experience Preferred Qualifications Preferred Experience: At least one year of clinical experience in audiology. At least one year of experience in the clinical supervision of SLP student Additional Information About Our School/Department Established in 1970, by the Board of Supervisors, the School of Allied Health Professions comprises both undergraduate and graduate programs. Baccalaureate degrees (Bachelor of Science) are offered in Cardiopulmonary Science and Medical Laboratory Science. The Department of Communication Disorders offers a Master of Communication Disorders degree in Speech and Language Pathology and a Doctor of Audiology (AuD) in hearing. The Department of Occupational Therapy offers the Master of Occupational Therapy Degree, the Department of Physical Therapy offers a Doctor of Physical Therapy degree, and the Department of Counseling offers the Master of Health Sciences degree. The SAHP also includes the Human Development Center, which provides programs to increase the capacity of healthcare providers for individuals with developmental and acquired disabilities. The SAHP provides multidisciplinary outpatient services to achieve diversity of patient objectives that include diagnostic, therapeutic, and restorative services to enable patients to achieve as much functional, social, and occupational independence as is reasonably possible. The School of Allied Health Professions is committed to providing quality education, leadership, research, and public service through direct patient care and community outreach by clinical healthcare professionals. Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c72026c5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUNO Communication Disorders (NO10516) LSUNO Communication Disorders (NO10516) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) e52fc1f1 Last Name (required) 3f296e78 Email (required) 37bc50c9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 7582299b Last Name (required) ffc23199 Email (required) e2614ff5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
