    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-a4cbe7fa-1bc1-46ea-9ea1-31f84cf385ee": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR 497384 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: Interdisciplinary Oncology Campus Location: CANCER CENTER Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Cancer Center is seeking faculty members who are committed to excellence in research that addresses biology and treatment of cancers that disproportionately burden the residents of Louisiana as we actively pursue NCI designation. Leveraging significant support from the State of Louisiana, Louisiana State University (LSU), our hospital partner, LCMC Health, and donors, we have a dynamic strategic plan that will achieve this goal. Faculty candidates should possess demonstrated expertise in (but not limited to) technological innovation, cancer-relevant molecular and cellular biology, genomics, epigenetics, infectious etiologies, tumor immunology, obesity, and/or cancer therapy development. An exceptional track record of accomplishments and sustained funding are preferred. Selected scientists will be offered competitive start-up funds commensurate with expertise and productivity. Rank and track to be determined by qualifications. Team recruitment will be considered for well-established investigators. Closely mentored research/career development programs are provided for ‘early-stage’ investigators. Incumbents will play a foundational role in defining the cancer research strategies, priorities, and implementation approaches within the State and the region directed toward NCI designation. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or MD Required Field of Study: Basic or Health Science or related field Substitution: PhD or MD equivalent, DVM, or MD/PhD are also acceptable. Degrees in other disciplines can be accepted with relevant research, experience, and/or funding. Preferred Experience: An exceptional track record of accomplishments and sustained funding are preferred Additional Information About This Position Louisiana is at the heart of the U.S. cancer burden with high incidence and mortality from most cancers, and faces significant challenges related to cancer care and health equity and disparities. However, for qualified, motivated, and innovative applicants, these challenges afford exceptional basic science and clinical translational opportunities directed toward NIH-designated priority areas. The Cancer Center has existing strengths in cancers of genitourinary, gastrointestinal, and hepatobiliary systems, and female reproductive tract, cancer biology, viral oncology, inflammation, immunology, obesity, and cancer metabolism. It combines clinical expertise, an exceptional clinical trials network, and a growing cadre of basic scientists to define underlying molecular mechanisms in cancer and derive novel interventions that improve prevention, early diagnosis, and treatment of cancer for our diverse populations. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Si