    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-clinical-primary-care-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, PRIMARY CARE",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, PRIMARY CARE - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, PRIMARY CARE - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, PRIMARY CARE 497406 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, PRIMARY CARE Employee Type: Faculty Department: Med-Comprehensive Medicine Campus Location: MEDICINE/NEW ORLEANS Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Comprehensive Medicine and Geriatrics in New Orleans, seeks a board certified / board eligible Primary Care Provider to join our faculty at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). The successful candidate will practice at University Medical Center – New Orleans (UMCNO) in a mix of teaching and non-teaching clinics. In all care areas, the successful candidate will maintain excellence in patient care, teaching, and research integrity. Academic appointment will be commensurate with professional achievement. Current trainees or junior faculty with an excellent track record are strongly encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: ABIM board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) physician in Internal Medicine; Licensed to practice medicine in the state of Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 63bb5333 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) caac4c54 Last Name (required) 02c507b2 Email (required) eb81c4c0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study p