    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-clinical-pulmonary-critical-care-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-d39f0a1e-bc9a-43d7-a3e6-3f795b34002d": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY CRITICAL CARE",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY CRITICAL CARE - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY CRITICAL CARE - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY CRITICAL CARE 497401 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY CRITICAL CARE Employee Type: Faculty Department: Med-Pulmonary/Critical Care Campus Location: MEDICINE/NEW ORLEANS Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Pulmonary and Critical Care in New Orleans, seeks a board certified / board eligible physician in Pulmonary Disease and Critical Care Medicine to join our faculty at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). This faculty member will practice at University Medical Center – New Orleans and will work in the ICU as well as the interstitial lung disease clinic, with a focus on developing a sarcoidosis center of excellence. Work as a general pulmonary consultant is also expected while their interstitial lung disease practice grows. In all care areas, the successful candidate will maintain excellence in patient care, teaching, and research integrity. Academic appointment will be commensurate with professional achievement. Current trainees or junior faculty with an excellent track record of inpatient and outpatient care proficiency are strongly encouraged to apply. Our group thrives on collaboration and looks forward to adding another team-oriented faculty member to our outstanding academic faculty group practice. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Completion of ACGME accredited Pulmonary CC fellowship Certifications or Licenses Required: ABIM board certified/board eligible in Pulmonary, Critical Care, and/or Interventional Pulmonary; licensed to practice medicine and credentialed with all required entities before start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e1c84d90 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Med-Nephrology (NO14924) Med-Nephrology (NO14924) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 61412337 Last Name (required) 9c77ce5b Email (required) 5cfbfee3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. D