    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-c7b750ca-1c7b-455b-9459-6e142bfc40b2": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR /ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR /ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR /ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR /ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR 497407 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Dentistry Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR /ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: LSUNO Oral Surgery Campus Location: ORAL SURGERY/DENTAL SCH/BOX 22 Job Summary/Basic Functions Louisiana State University Health Science Center is seeking applicants for faculty positions in the Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery department. This is a faculty position at the Assistant, Associate or Professor level, based in New Orleans. The OMS department’s primary responsibilities are providing didactic instruction and clinical supervision for dental students, residents, non-categorical interns, externs, and medical students at the LSU School of Dentistry and affiliated hospital clinics and ORs, as well as meeting the OMS treatment needs of the community. This faculty role will provide comprehensive OMS care—including dentoalveolar procedures, implants, orthognathic surgery, trauma management, and pathology treatment—while supporting resident education, multidisciplinary collaboration, and high-volume clinical operations in an academic-focused environment. The ideal candidate must demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, mentoring, leadership, patient care, service, and scholarship. Proficiency in facial trauma surgery is critical. A record of scholarly activity is desirable, and the pursuit of scholarly activity is expected. Numerous opportunities for collaboration exist within the school of dentistry and the LSU Health Science Center in New Orleans. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Other Information About the Position Our 6-year integrated OMS – MD residency program is regarded as one of the busiest and best CODA-accredited training programs in the country. The department has a long history of recruiting quality students/residents and graduating top-rated clinicians. Candidates will also have the option to participate in the Faculty Practice and provide call coverage at our affiliated hospitals and the LSU School of Dentistry. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: DDS/DMD Required Field of Study: completion of an accredited OMS residency program Certifications or Licenses Required: Must be eligible for full licensure to practice Dentistry in the State of Louisiana and Certified, or Board Eligible by the American Board of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery; BLS; ACLS; PALS by start date. Number of years required to perform the job: 0 Type of experience required to perform the job: Hospital-based, OMS clinic, or academic practice; hands-on experience in dentoalveolar surgery, dental implants, orthognathic corrections, facial trauma reconstruction, and maxillofacial pathology. Board eligibility or certification. Preferred Qualifications Other Education if applicable: fellowship training in Orthognathic/TMJ Surgery, Facial Cosmetics, Craniofacial Surgery, or Head and Neck Oncologic Surgery and Microsurgical Reconstruction Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 8dd8d572 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUNO Oral Surgery (NO12260) LSUNO Oral Surgery (NO12260) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 2ca26e87 Last Name (required) 60b63a4f Email (required) c20d3c95 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) f46f5119 Last Name (required) a8a53b5f Email (required) 53ea61fe Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)