    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor-clinical-psychiatry-baton-rouge-louisiana-united-states-2478451a-7719-4b49-ac67-ab8c25411447": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY 497376 Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY Employee Type: Faculty Department: EKLMC-Psychiatry Campus Location: EKLMC/PSYCHIATRY/FACULTY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Psychiatry of the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) School of Medicine in Baton Rouge is seeking candidates for academic faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) to serve as Child and Adolescent Psychiatrists for the Baton Rouge Campus. Incumbents will serve as core faculty for the Child and Adolescent Psychiatry Fellowship Program. This position will include academic duties and psychiatric services at teaching hospital(s) and/or directly in the outpatient clinical settings. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Fellowship Training Required Field of Study: Child and Adolescent Psychiatry Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent); Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benef