      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY 497370 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Psychiatry Campus Location: PSYCHIATRY/PAID/FACULTY/STAFF Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Psychiatry of the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) School of Medicine at New Orleans is seeking an Adult Psychiatry faculty at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) to work in the New Orleans Area. The successful candidate will have demonstrated expertise in clinical work in an inpatient setting. An interest in providing Collaborative Agreement support for APPs is required. In addition to staffing the inpatient unit with direct patient care, the incumbent will participate in nights and weekend tele call consult to the APPs onsite. This is an excellent opportunity to be an integral part of a new initiative to expand mental health services to the New Orleans community with a newly constructed inpatient psychiatry unit at New Orleans East Hospital. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Required Field of Study: General Psychiatry Certifications or Licenses Required: ABPN Board Certified or eligible (or equivalent) in Psychiatry; Licensed to practice in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities by start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a656a6b3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Psychiatry (NO14965) Psychiatry (NO14965) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) feb444f3 Last Name (required) bb68edff Email (required) 86350d2b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the