    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-or-associate-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-e6da6c72-74bc-4cc5-b7f9-929c87b06fa9": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR 497347 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: LSUNO Physiology Campus Location: PHYSIOLOGY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Physiology in the School of Medicine at LSU Health Sciences Center in New Orleans, LA invites applications for an academic faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor from outstanding candidates with a Ph.D. or M.D. (or equivalent) degree. Rank and track to be determined based on candidate's qualifications. Special consideration will be given to candidates with a demonstrated record of excellent research accomplishments in the physiological mechanisms underlying alcohol and drug misuse, and with the willingness and ability to contribute teaching programs for graduate, undergraduate and health care professionals in training. The successful applicant will have a joint appointment in the Alcohol and Drug Abuse Center of Excellence, and he/she will be expected to synergize with existing research strengths in these areas. Applicants are also expected to maintain an active, extramural-funded research program, and to mentor students and research fellows. Opportunities are available for interaction with the Centers of Excellence in Cancer, Neuroscience, Cardiovascular Biology, and Burn, which are supported by a state-of-the-art infrastructure including access to core laboratories in genomics, proteomics, imaging, and flow cytometry. The position will be supported by designated laboratory space, competitive salary and start-up package. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD, MD, or equivalent Required Field of Study: Physiology, Neuroscience, Pharmacology, or Cell Biology Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dfea4a9f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUNO Physiology (NO11035) LSUNO Physiology (NO11035) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) fb278016 Last Name (required) a92ddd9b Email (required) b8746a8f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS)