    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-hospital-medicine-baton-rouge-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, HOSPITAL MEDICINE",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, HOSPITAL MEDICINE - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, HOSPITAL MEDICINE - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, HOSPITAL MEDICINE 497359 Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, HOSPITAL MEDICINE Employee Type: Faculty Department: EKLMC-Medicine Campus Location: EKLMC/MEDICINE/FACULTY Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Medicine is accepting applications for an academic faculty position in the field of Internal Medicine. The position is based at LSU Health Baton Rouge and is affiliated with Our Lady of the Lake Regional Medical Center. The responsibilities will include direct patient care, teaching medical students, residents, and fellows, and research. The Internal Medicine Hospitalist provides comprehensive inpatient medical care to adult patients at Our Lady of the Lake Hospital, managing acute and chronic medical conditions and coordinating care with multidisciplinary teams. The position also supports clinical education and collaboration with residents, medical students, and other healthcare professionals while promoting high-quality, evidence-based patient care. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible in Internal Medicine (or equivalent); Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert db0e4002 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUHSC Unit-Earl K Long Medcia (NO14982) LSUHSC Unit-Earl K Long Medcia (NO14982) Locations Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 582bdcb4 Last Name (required) dd503f67 Email (required) dda96a20 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 61c2d713 Last Name (required) 362177df Email (required) afc0871e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
