    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-hematology-oncology-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-8e88d45a-335c-4fa5-8365-fe5bcd755e84": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY 497324 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Med-Hematology and oncology Campus Location: MEDICINE/NEW ORLEANS Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Medicine, Section of Hematology-Oncology in New Orleans, LA, seeks a mix of clinicians and clinician-investigators or clinician-scientists in the areas of malignant hematology, bone marrow transplant and cellular therapy, solid tumor oncology and general hematology/oncology. Academic appointments will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor; both tenured and non-tenured/clinical tracks are available, with rank and track dependent on qualifications. These unique positions offer candidates an exciting opportunity to practice academic clinical oncology in conjunction with research appointments in the LSU LCMC Health Cancer Center. Research support will be available for candidates with demonstrated success as a clinician-scientist. The new faculty recruitment is an important part of the LSU LCMC Health Cancer Center’s mission to achieve National Cancer Institute (NCI) Designated Cancer Center status, and in their journey of reimagining and transforming cancer care in New Orleans regions, and the State of Louisiana. Robust transdisciplinary research opportunities and support would be available across the campuses of LSU and within the Cancer Center. Candidates with expertise and experience in Malignant Hematology, BMT and Cellular Therapy, Breast, GI, GU Oncology, Melanoma and Soft Tissues/Sarcoma are particularly encouraged to apply. Additionally, candidates with strong interest and experience in clinical trials including investigator-initiated trials, and clinical-translational research are highly desirable. Candidates should be board-certified or eligible for American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM) Hematology and/or Medical Oncology certification, or its equivalent at the time of appointment. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: ABIM board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) physician in Hematology and/or Medical Oncology; Licensed to practice medicine in the state of Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire Additional Information About Our School/Department LSU Health Sciences Center is located in beautiful New Orleans, Louisiana. It is the home of 6 schools and 13 Centers of Excellence. The LSUHSC School of Medicine is currently expanding its relationships with its academic clinical partners. As a result, leadership roles within our clinical and research activities are available. Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e89d3afa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select 