    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-clinical-pulmonary-critical-care-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-CLINICAL PULMONARY/CRITICAL CARE",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-CLINICAL PULMONARY/CRITICAL CARE - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-CLINICAL PULMONARY/CRITICAL CARE - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-CLINICAL PULMONARY/CRITICAL CARE 497237 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR-CLINICAL PULMONARY/CRITICAL CARE Employee Type: Faculty Department: Med-Pulmonary/Critical Care Me Campus Location: MEDICINE/NEW ORLEANS Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Pulmonary and Critical Care in New Orleans, seeks a board certified / board eligible Interventional Pulmonologist (IP) to join our faculty at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). Having completed an ACGME accredited IP fellowship, the successful candidate will practice at University Medical Center – New Orleans (UMCNO). The candidate will be responsible for performing all diagnostic and therapeutic procedures that are needed at UMCNO and fall within the scope their IP training. Duties as a critical care physician in the ICU as well as a pulmonary consultant are also anticipated while the faculty’s IP practice grows. In all care areas, the successful candidate will maintain excellence in patient care, teaching, and research integrity. Academic appointment will be commensurate with professional achievement. Current trainees or junior faculty with an excellent track record of IP procedural proficiency are strongly encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Completion of ACGME accredited Interventional Pulmonology fellowship Certifications or Licenses Required: ABIM board certified/board eligible in Pulmonary, Critical Care, and/or Interventional Pulmonary; licensed to practice medicine and credentialed with all required entities before start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 5a1e6bb1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Med-Nephrology (NO14924) Med-Nephrology (NO14924) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 0a25f2f8 Last Name (required) c247e4ae Email (required) 4a5e0b22 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 924b052d Last Name (required) e034ee55 Email (required) 47a4ff66 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
