    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-psychology-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHOLOGY 497238 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Psychiatry Campus Location: PSYCHIATRY/PAID/FACULTY/STAFF Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Psychiatry of the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) School of Medicine in New Orleans is a seeking candidate for an academic faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) to provide adult psychological services as a clinician and provide trauma-informed evaluation and psychotherapy services to survivors of violent crime and traumatic injury. The candidate will provide clinical supervision, consultation and training to staff and trainees on trauma-informed, evidence-based interventions. The candidate will also be involved in program development and research at the University Medical Center New Orleans (UMC) Level One Trauma Center. The position is housed in the UMC Trauma Recovery Center which is designed to help survivors of violent crime and traumatic injury overcome barriers to accessing mental health treatment, health care, and legal resources in the acute aftermath of trauma. The center works collaboratively across psychology, psychiatry, social work, trauma surgery, hospital-based and clinic-based violence intervention programs, and community partners. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or equivalent Required Field of Study: Clinical Psychology Certifications or Licenses Required: Licensed to practice in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities by start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 52286620 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Psychiatry (NO14965) Psychiatry (NO14965) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 1854c7e0 Last Name (required) 1f2b9df6 Email (required) dd6123ad Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Superv