    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-orthopaedics-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-a8d6f94c-8281-4820-a1c4-d93ba2bacc62": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, ORTHOPAEDICS",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, ORTHOPAEDICS - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, ORTHOPAEDICS - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, ORTHOPAEDICS 497037 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, ORTHOPAEDICS Employee Type: Faculty Department: Orthopedics Campus Location: ORTHOPAEDICS Job Summary/Basic Functions LSU Health-NO Orthopaedics is currently seeking qualified applicants for an academic, orthopaedic joint arthroplasty surgeon to work with LSUHSC Orthopaedics at University Medical Center – New Orleans (UMCNO). Appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). Incumbent will develop a comprehensive joint program for UMCNO and LSUHSC and will participate in resident education and research efforts for LSU Orthopaedics. The ideal candidate will have an interest in traumaplasty. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Graduate of an accredited orthopaedic joint fellowship before hire date Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent); Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits inc