    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-or-associate-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR 497026 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OR ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence (NO1497700) Campus Location: 449920000 - Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence Job Summary/Basic Functions The Cardiovascular Center of Excellence in the School of Medicine at LSU Health Sciences Center in New Orleans, LA is seeking candidates for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. Candidates should have an active extramurally-funded grant, the desire to participate in collaborative research projects related to cardiovascular research and teaching ability. Exceptional unfunded applicants will also be considered. Expertise in all areas of cardiovascular research will be considered, but special consideration will be given to those that complement the existing collaborative research strengths of the Center which include Heart Failure, Hypertension and Autonomic Regulation. The Cardiovascular Center of Excellence and LSUHSC-NO School of Medicine provide investigators with a scientific environment conducive to research success, with state-of-the-art Core Laboratories including Proteomics, Imaging, Cardiovascular Function, RNA and DNA Sequencing, Flow Cytometry, and Animal Care facilities. Opportunities are available for interaction with other Centers of Excellence in Neuroscience, Alcohol Research and Cancer. Anticipated duties and responsibilities will include sustaining an exceptional research program, mentoring of graduate students/post-doctoral fellows, and participating in the broad health sciences teaching activities of the Center. The institution offers competitive start-up packages and salaries. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or MD Required Field of Study: Basic Science, Health Science, or Related Field Preferred Education: PhD or MD Preferred Discipline: Basic Science, Health Science, or Related Field Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ef4eea87 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence (NO14977) Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence (NO14977) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) ba059b81 Last Name (required) c5cc6a2b Email (required) e87d96ab Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 9e52045f Last Name (required) 54c91eb4 Email (required) e029db65 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
