    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor-clinical-psychiatry-baton-rouge-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY 496857 Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR, OR PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PSYCHIATRY Employee Type: Faculty Department: EKLMC-Psychiatry Campus Location: EKLMC/PSYCHIATRY/FACULTY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Section of Psychiatry in Baton Rouge is seeking an addiction psychiatrist for a clinical faculty position. The incumbent will provide psychiatric care to patients in an outpatient and inpatient settings, including evaluation, diagnosis, treatment planning, and medication management. Responsibilities include delivering longitudinal outpatient care, coordinating with multidisciplinary team members, and supporting continuity of care. Participation in call coverage, including nights and weekends, may be required. The role also includes teaching and supervision of medical students, residents, and fellows, with opportunities to contribute to educational programs. The successful candidate will work collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team and support the ongoing development of clinical services. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent); Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ed5500f4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUHSC Unit-Earl K Long Medcia (NO14982) LSUHSC Unit-Earl K Long Medcia (NO14982) Locations Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) da6fd639 Last Name (required) 6b56185f Email (required) a16f41e3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected 