    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-trauma-critical-care-surgery-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-9010aa91-09cd-4e2a-a6c3-3a476e940653": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - TRAUMA/CRITICAL CARE SURGERY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - TRAUMA/CRITICAL CARE SURGERY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - TRAUMA/CRITICAL CARE SURGERY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - TRAUMA/CRITICAL CARE SURGERY 496998 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - TRAUMA/CRITICAL CARE SURGERY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Surgery Campus Location: SURGERY/FULL TIME Job Summary/Basic Functions The Louisiana State University (LSU) School of Medicine’s Department of Surgery is seeking a faculty member to work in Trauma / Critical Care Surgery at University Medical Center - New Orleans (UMCNO). This program is part of the highly regarded Norman E. McSwain, Jr., M.D., Spirit of Charity Level I Trauma Center at UMC. The faculty appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Rank and appointment track will be determined based on qualifications, experience, and stature in the field. The successful applicant must demonstrate a high degree of expertise in trauma / critical care management, as well as leadership experience. This individual will be involved in teaching Surgical Critical Care fellows, General Surgery residents, and medical students. An established record of scholarly activity is expected. A successful applicant should have a history of working well with others with a reasonable degree of affability and clinical availability. There are leadership opportunities within the department and also within the clinical partner hospital administration for candidates with leadership and management experience. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: BC/BE (or equivalent) surgeon in General Surgery and in Surgical Critical Care; must be licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before date of hire Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 2247274d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Surgery (NO14972) Surgery (NO14972) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 41d3ea14 Last Name (required) aca5738b Email (required) 970beaec Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 272fec7f Last Name (required) d3241fd3 Email (required) 8cdbbd02 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
