    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/associate-professor-or-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR 496979 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: Neurosurgery Campus Location: NEUROSURGERY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Neurosurgery and Stanley S. Scott Cancer Research Center of Excellence of the School of Medicine, LSU Health Sciences Center – New Orleans invite applications for an academic faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor; rank and track to be determined based on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Interested candidates should have an active and significant extramurally funded program and a vision for collaborative research projects related to cancer research and drug development. Reporting to the Department Head of Neurosurgery, this faculty position will be a member of the Neurosurgery Department with a joint appointment with the LSU-LCMC Health Cancer Center. The candidate will have an opportunity to collaborate in research partnerships across LSU campuses, including, Pennington Biomedical Research Center, and LCMC Health. We are seeking applications from distinguished academicians with proven scientific, strategic and collaborative leadership skills. The successful candidate should be committed to the development of leading research with a focus on extramural grant funding and academic excellence in support of the research and educational missions of the institution, and a commitment to excellence in academics including mentoring residents and medical students. Incumbent will be expected to generate successful funding ventures, leveraging the talents of faculty, staff, and trainees. Qualified applicants should have a record of scholarship commensurate with appointment as Associate Professor or Professor; international reputation and track record of success in some aspect of cellular and molecular medicine; a demonstrated commitment to excellence in academics including medical, graduate and post-graduate education and the mentoring of trainees and faculty; and promoting the development of innovative research programs that align with the research mission of the School of Medicine and the Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center New Orleans. Applicants must demonstrate strong commitment to scholarly research that complement our existing and growing areas of research in brain tumors. Mid-career and senior scholars with an interest in drug development like utilizing antibodies and genetically engineered variants against tumor-specific antigens and drug delivery and are specially encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or MD Type of experience required to perform the job: Qualified for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 60578866 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Neurosurgery (NO14930) Neurosurgery (NO14930) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) f0da8073 Last Name (required) 88ecf010 Email (required) 98c9fa75 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) e8a5cc8d Last Name (required) c1a26867 Email (required) 146d4f80 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
