    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-0bd1b5d9-c6a6-424c-bcc6-ce7b66ffcf77": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR 496945 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: Interdisciplinary Oncology Campus Location: CANCER CENTER/SETON BLDG./2025 Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Cancer Center is seeking faculty members who are committed to excellence in research that addresses biology and treatment of cancers that disproportionately burden the residents of Louisiana as we actively pursue NCI designation. Leveraging significant support from the State of Louisiana, Louisiana State University (LSU), our hospital partner, LCMC Health, and donors, we have a dynamic strategic plan that will achieve this goal. Faculty candidates should possess demonstrated expertise in (but not limited to) technological innovation, cancer-relevant molecular and cellular biology, genomics, epigenetics, infectious etiologies, tumor immunology, obesity, and/or cancer therapy development. An exceptional track record of accomplishments and sustained funding are preferred. Selected scientists will be offered competitive start-up funds commensurate with expertise and productivity. Rank and track to be determined by qualifications. Team recruitment will be considered for well-established investigators. Closely mentored research/career development programs are provided for ‘early-stage’ investigators. Incumbents will play a foundational role in defining the cancer research strategies, priorities, and implementation approaches within the State and the region directed toward NCI designation. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or MD Required Field of Study: Basic or Health Science or related field Substitution: PhD or MD equivalent, DVM, or MD/PhD are also acceptable. Degrees in other disciplines can be accepted with relevant research, experience, and/or funding. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Experience: An exceptional track record of accomplishments and sustained funding are preferred. Additional Information About This Position Louisiana is at the heart of the U.S. cancer burden with high incidence and mortality from most cancers, and faces significant challenges related to cancer care and health equity and disparities. However, for qualified, motivated, and innovative applicants, these challenges afford exceptional basic science and clinical translational opportunities directed toward NIH-designated priority areas. The Cancer Center has existing strengths in cancers of genitourinary, gastrointestinal, and hepatobiliary systems, and female reproductive tract, cancer biology, viral oncology, inflammation, immunology, obesity, and cancer metabolism. It combines clinical expertise, an exceptional clinical trials network, and a growing cadre of basic scientists to define underlying molecular mechanisms in cancer and derive novel interventions that improve prevention, early diagnosis, and treatment of cancer for our diverse populations. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e43a7cf3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) d92fc9f9 Last Name (required) 82a034b6 Email (required) e1d2c90e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 94743bbd Last Name (required) 6c396810 Email (required) 182acbe3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/instructor-part-time-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "INSTRUCTOR - PART-TIME",
      "description": "INSTRUCTOR - PART-TIME - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States INSTRUCTOR - PART-TIME - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! INSTRUCTOR - PART-TIME 496927 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Nursing Add to favorites View favorites Title: INSTRUCTOR - PART-TIME Employee Type: Faculty Department: Adult Nursing Campus Location: NURSING - ADULT Job Summary/Basic Functions LSU Health New Orleans School of Nursing is seeking a highly motivated individual to join our faculty as a school of nursing excellence within an academic health sciences center environment. Our nursing faculty have the opportunity to educate future nurses at the BSN, MN/MSN, DNS and DNP level, including state-of-the-art simulation laboratories; conduct nursing & interdisciplinary research; engage in faculty practice, including our nurse-run clinics; pursue entrepreneurial and consultative activities; and serve as a nursing leader and development of leadership skills through our Emergent Nurse Leader Program. We invite you to submit your curriculum vitae for the following teaching positions: Adult Health, Mental Health, Medical Surgical, Pediatrics, Community Health, Primary Care (FNP), Women’s Health. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Master's Required Field of Study: Nursing (limited exceptions) Certifications or Licenses Required: Louisiana Registered Nurse (RN) licensure (by start date). Preferred Qualifications Preferred Education: Doctorate Preferred Discipline: Candidates pursuing a career in Nursing Research. Certifications or Licenses Preferred: Advanced Practice Certification (APRN) Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7fd51aac Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Adult Nursing (formerly: Assoc (NO15510) Adult Nursing (formerly: Assoc (NO15510) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) e55f38ba Last Name (required) cee296f1 Email (required) 72934949 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 499e760d Last Name (required) 41d42ac2 Email (required) 3941deb4 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
