    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-research-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states-052df926-469f-4598-b07c-cba1ae64dd52": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH 496867 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH Employee Type: Faculty Department: LSUNO Genetics Campus Location: GENETICS Job Summary/Basic Functions Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) -School of Medicine’s Bioinformatics and Computational Medicine (BCM) Training Program in the Department of Genetics invites applications for a junior faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor - Research, in the field of bioinformatics and computation medicine. This is an exciting opportunity for a talented candidate to contribute to training the next generation of scientists and physician scientists and conducting groundbreaking research in the fields of bioinformatics, computational medicine, Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence with application to biomedical research. The successful candidate will work in a highly collaborative and supportive environment, working closely with a multidisciplinary team of bioinformaticians, basic and translational researchers to advance the research, education and service missions of the School of Medicine. The successful candidate will: (1) Be involved in teaching courses, training and mentoring graduate students enrolled in the MS Bioinformatics Track and medical students enrolled in the MD/MS Computational Medicine Track. The successful candidate will serve as Assistant Director to the Director of the BCM Training Program, providing strategic and technology solutions, developing education and training as well as maintaining the software and technology infrastructure critical to the development and advancement of the training program. (2). Be involved in conducting biomedical research focused on development and application of advanced bioinformatics and computation genomics methods and algorithms specifically, Machine Learning and AI with application to analysis and integration of large-scale multi-omics data, modelling complex gene regulatory networks and predicting disease threats. In the long term, it is expected that the successful candidate will develop an independent line of research and source funding. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD Required Field of Study: Bioinformatics, Computational Genomics, Computer Science, computer engineering or closely related field Number of years required to perform the job: 1 Type of experience required to perform the job: Demonstrated experience supported by a publication record in bioinformatics, computational genomics, Machine Learning and AI. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Education: PhD Preferred Discipline: Bioinformatics, Computational Genomics, Computer Science, computer engineering or closely related field. Preferred Experience: -PhD 1-2 years postdoc with experience supported by a strong publication record in bioinformatics and computational genomics. -Demonstrated experience in multiplatform multiscale multi-omics data analysis and integration. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! 