    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-obstetrics-and-gynecology-baton-rouge-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY - Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY 496898 Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Campus Location: OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is seeking applications for an academic faculty position to serve as Residency Program Director position at Woman’s Hospital in Baton Rouge, LA. Appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (clinical, non-tenure track). In addition to administrative duties, this candidate will provide clinical coverage in obstetrics and gynecology and relevant specialties, as appropriate and based on training. Qualified candidates will be very familiar with quality and safety initiatives and will ideally have experience with managing residency programs and schedules The Residency Program Director will participate in departmental and hospital committees and activities as outlined by the Department of OB/GYN Chair. The new Program Director will designate 50% of time to clinical work and 50% of time to the administrative duties as Program Director. Must be Board Certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology and licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana before hire date. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board Certified in ObGyn; licensed to practice medicine in LA and credentialed with all required entities before hire date. Number of years required to perform the job: minimum of three years of educational and/or administrative experience Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 129e6207 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Obstetrics and Gynecology (NO14933) Obstetrics and Gynecology (NO14933) Locations Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States Baton Rouge, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 9ca4043d Last Name (required) 6f2ddb7b Email (required) 7f0c5ea8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 0ee74796 Last Name (required) 564f02ef Email (required) b9c4da98 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
