    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR 496883 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Dentistry Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR Employee Type: Faculty Department: LSUNO Orthodontics Campus Location: ORTHODONTICS/DENTAL SCH/BOX 23 Job Summary/Basic Functions The Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) School of Dentistry in New Orleans invites applications for an immediate opening as a full-time, tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Orthodontics. The department has a strong pre-doctoral and post-doctoral curriculum. We are seeking an outstanding educator who will engage in didactic pre-clinical and clinical instruction for undergraduate dental, dental hygiene and postgraduate students, as well as in research activity. Opportunity to participate in the dental school’s faculty practice is also available. Candidates must possess outstanding academic credentials, excellent oral and written communication skills. A record of scholarly achievement (required for tenured/tenure track position) and experience teaching and mentoring students is preferred. Applicants must have a Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS), Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) or equivalent degree, and a certificate of Advanced Education in Orthodontics and Dentofacial Orthopedics from a program accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA); American Board of Orthodontics (ABO) certification is highly preferred. The successful candidate should be eligible for licensure by the Louisiana State Board of Dentistry. Academic appointment and salary will be commensurate with training and experience. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: DDS/DMD Other Education if applicable: Certificate in Orthodontics Preferred Qualifications Other Education if applicable: Diplomate of the American Board of Orthodontics Preferred Discipline: Orthodontics and Dentofacial Orthopedics Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a2a570fe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUNO Orthodontics (NO12265) LSUNO Orthodontics (NO12265) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) cc2a2267 Last Name (required) f5d43e52 Email (required) ddc83bc0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) fa12a211 Last Name (required) 367d242c Email (required) a2c88515 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
