      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR- HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR- HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR- HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY 496444 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR- HEMATOLOGY ONCOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Med-Hematology and oncology Campus Location: MEDICINE/NEW ORLEANS Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Medicine, Section of Hematology-Oncology in New Orleans, LA, seeks three (3) enthusiastic and dynamic oncology clinician-scientists. Academic appointments will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor; both tenured and non-tenured/clinical tracks are available, with rank and track dependent on qualifications. These unique positions offer candidates an opportunity to practice academic clinical oncology in conjunction with research appointments in the LSU LCMC Health Cancer Center. Research support will be available for candidates with demonstrated success as a clinician scientist. LSU Health Sciences Center is located in beautiful New Orleans, Louisiana. It is the home of 6 schools and 13 Centers of Excellence. The LSUHSC School of Medicine is currently expanding its relationships with its academic clinical partners. As a result, leadership roles within our clinical and research activities are available. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: ABIM board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) physician in Hematology and/or Medical Oncology; Licensed to practice medicine in the state of Louisiana before hire Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to