    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-family-medicine-bogalusa-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE - Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE - Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE 496643 Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States, 70427 Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE Employee Type: Faculty Department: Family Medicine Campus Location: Family Medi/Bogalusa/Residents Job Summary/Basic Functions Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) Rural Family Medicine Residency program in Bogalusa, LA seeks a board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) family medicine physician for faculty appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). The ideal candidate will have previous academic experience, though not required. Practice highlights: •Primary responsibilities include precepting the LSUHSC Rural Family Medicine Residency program. We are an institutionally sponsored, fully accredited program currently expanding from 18-21 residents. •Academic faculty appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track); rank to be commensurate with physician’s credentials and experience. •Position includes an outpatient only option or a traditional inpatient/outpatient practice •Inpatient responsibilities at Our Lady of Angels Hospital Other Information About the Position Community highlights: •Bogalusa, Louisiana is located ninety minutes north of New Orleans with a population 13,000. •An outdoor adventurist’s dream, you’ll experience a small-town feel with big-city conveniences! •Beautiful communities like Covington and Mandeville, excellent schools, a low cost of living, and affordable housing make Bogalusa a wonderful place for your family to call home. •Nicknamed the “Big Easy”, New Orleans is one of the world’s most fascinating cities and home to a truly unique melting pot of culture and tradition with great food and music. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent); Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire Preferred Qualifications Preferred Experience: Previous academic experience Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c761535d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Family Medicine (NO14915) Family Medicine (NO14915) Locations Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 258bfd72 Last Name (required) f305097d Email (required) 1f717c2c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) ba3fcae9 Last Name (required) bb4a860f Email (required) 8542a5fd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
