    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-gen-internal-med-lafayette-lafayette-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, GEN INTERNAL MED, LAFAYETTE",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, GEN INTERNAL MED, LAFAYETTE - Lafayette, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, GEN INTERNAL MED, LAFAYETTE - Lafayette, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, GEN INTERNAL MED, LAFAYETTE 496553 Lafayette, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, GEN INTERNAL MED, LAFAYETTE Employee Type: Faculty Department: UMC-Medicine Campus Location: MED - University Hosp & Clinic Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center (LSUHSC) School of Medicine is seeking an outstanding academic physician for a General Internal Medicine faculty position in the Department of Medicine in Lafayette, LA. Responsibilities include patient care and participation in the education of residents, fellows and medical students. A commitment to teaching is required in order to provide outstanding instruction to medical students and residents in various clinical venues. Academic appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track), and will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience and record of academic achievement. LSU Health offers a competitive salary and benefits package. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) in Medicine; Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert b997f0ba Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments LSUHSC Unit-Earl K Long Medcia (NO14982) LSUHSC Unit-Earl K Long Medcia (NO14982) Locations Lafayette, Louisiana, United States Lafayette, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 1b75abe8 Last Name (required) 241f055c Email (required) 03a31f94 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected