    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/instructor-assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-family-medicine-bogalusa-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "INSTRUCTOR / ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE",
      "description": "INSTRUCTOR / ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE - Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States INSTRUCTOR / ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE - Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! INSTRUCTOR / ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, FAMILY MEDICINE 496584 Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States, 70427 Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: INSTRUCTOR / ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL FAMILY MEDICINE Employee Type: Faculty Department: Family Medicine Campus Location: Family Medi/Bogalusa/Residents Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Family Medicine of the LSU Health Sciences Center – New Orleans is seeking applications for an academic faculty position to serve as a Behavioral Health Specialist/Educator. This position is based in Bogalusa, LA. Appointment will be at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track), dependent on qualifications. Incumbent will be a vital member of the Family Medicine Residency Program, providing expertise in the integration of behavioral health principles and practices within the primary care setting. The Behavioral Health Specialist/Educator will share responsibilities with the Program Director and other faculty for the design and implementation of the behavioral health curriculum, ensuring residents receive training sufficient to meet and exceed the Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education Program Requirements for the residency program. Incumbent will focus on various domains including behavioral and community health, human behavior, psychiatry, ethics, doctor-patient communication, cultural humility, quality improvement, interdisciplinary approach, and well-being (for residents and faculty). Such training occurs during specialized didactic presentations, during rotations, one-on-one or group sessions with residents, and longitudinally while co-precepting with faculty physicians. The Behavioral Health Specialist/Educator will engage in scholarly activities within the Family Medicine Residency Program. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: PhD or PsyD in Clinical Psychology from an APA-accredited institution, and successful completion of an APA-accredited clinical internship or residency program Required Field of Study: must be licensed to practice clinical psychology in Louisiana by start date Preferred Experience: Experience in population health, quality improvement, and statistical analysis is a plus Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e7158332 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Family Medicine (NO14915) Family Medicine (NO14915) Locations Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States Bogalusa, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 22c60cb3 Last Name (required) 08169e2a Email (required) 9b660845 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) c39c2a57 Last Name (required) 4d127a15 Email (required) 73622048 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL 496589 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL Employee Type: Faculty Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Campus Location: OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology of the LSU Health New Orleans is seeking a fellowship-trained Urogynecologic surgeon for an academic faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). Urogynecology Division Directorship may be available for the appropriate qualified individual. The primary focus of the Urogynecologist will be the clinical care of urogynecologic patients, supervision and teaching of urogynecology academic fellows, ob-gyn residents, and medical students, and conducting of clinical research. In addition, participation in research and scholarly activities is expected. Clinical responsibilities will include urogynecologic office practice, office-based procedures, and inpatient and outpatient urogynecologic surgery. The successful applicant will demonstrate an aptitude for and dedication to medical education including direct teaching of medical students, residents and fellows. Full participation in all LSU OBGYN Departmental activities is expected. Qualified applicants must be licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana before the date of hire and be Board Certified/Board Eligible in OBGYN and Urogynecologic Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS). Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board Certified/Board Eligible (or equivalent) in OBGYN & URPS; Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana before hire Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 5ab84301 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Obstetrics and Gynecology (NO14933) Obstetrics and Gynecology (NO14933) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) e2860eef Last Name (required) 32fc740c Email (required) 4085bbad Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Canc