    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-radiology-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL RADIOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL RADIOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL RADIOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL RADIOLOGY 496581 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, RADIOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Radiology Campus Location: RADIOLOGY/SUPPORT STAFF Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Radiology of the LSU Health Sciences Center School of Medicine in New Orleans seeks an affable physician for an academic faculty position in the Emergency Radiology division at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Full Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). Fellowship training will be considered a plus but is not required. Our department is dedicated to excellence in patient care, education and scholarly activity. International candidates with exceptional training and background or seeking J-1 waiver are encouraged to apply. We provide multi-modality radiology services for University Medical Center – New Orleans. This is a state-of-the-art facility supporting 300+ beds and the only Level 1 Trauma Center in South Louisiana, the Norman E. McSwain, Jr, MD, Spirit of Charity Trauma Center. We are a collegial group looking for someone interested in working predominantly an ER shift from 8p-8a. This is a wonderful opportunity for a radiologist to practice cutting edge radiology in a stimulating and challenging environment, with manageable study volume. Please do not be deterred by academic responsibilities. Strong clinical skills are the priority as is a genuine interest in sharing clinical knowledge with residents. We are offering a very competitive salary with additional pay for evening hours. Qualified candidates must be ABR certified or on the pathway to full board certification and licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana before hire date. Other Information About the Position Position Highlights Collegial group practicing in a stimulating and challenging environment Ample opportunities to engage in clinical research and scholarship Previous academic experience is not required. Academic rank will be determined in accordance with School of Medicine and LSU System criteria. Robust Compensation and Benefits: Competitive salary Choice of retirement plans (defined benefit or defined contribution) Supplemental retirement plans (403(b) and 457(b)) Malpractice insurance including tail Health insurance supplemented and premiums pretax Other pretax benefits, subsidized insurances and group discounts Generous vacation, holiday and conference time Relocation incentive payment Flexible schedules for a healthy work-life balance For more benefits see: https://www.lsuhsc.edu/administration/hrm/benefits-about.aspx Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: ABR certified or on the pathway to full-board certification; Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 01f8c478 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Radiology (NO14971) Radiology (NO14971) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 91b41227 Last Name (required) 75c87e47 Email (required) 34e681ab Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 363c4138 Last Name (required) 34845fe6 Email (required) 2a2143d5 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
