    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/instructor-or-assistant-professor-nurse-anesthesia-program-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR-NURSE ANESTHESIA PROGRAM",
      "description": "INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR-NURSE ANESTHESIA PROGRAM - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR-NURSE ANESTHESIA PROGRAM - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR-NURSE ANESTHESIA PROGRAM 496558 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Nursing Add to favorites View favorites Title: INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR-NURSE ANESTHESIA PROGRAM Employee Type: Faculty Department: Nursing CRNA Program Campus Location: Nursing CRNA Program Job Summary/Basic Functions LSU Health New Orleans School of Nursing is seeking a highly motivated individual to join our faculty as a school of nursing excellence within an academic health sciences center environment. Our nursing faculty have the opportunity to educate future nurses at the BSN, MN/MSN, PhD and DNP level, including state-of-the-art simulation laboratories; conduct nursing & interdisciplinary research; engage in faculty practice, including our nurse-run clinics; pursue entrepreneurial and consultative activities; and serve as a nursing leader and development of leadership skills through our Emergent Nurse Leader Program. We invite you to submit your curriculum vitae for the following teaching position: Nurse Anesthesia Program Faculty. Candidates with expertise with diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong record of developmental research achievement, enthusiasm for teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and experience and commitment to teaching and mentoring individuals from diverse ethnic, socioeconomic, and cultural backgrounds. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Doctorate Other Education if applicable: Doctorate of Nursing Practice Certifications or Licenses Required: Licensed or eligible for licensure in Louisiana as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (Licensure by Start Date), currently certified/re-certified by the Council on Certification of Nurse Anesthetists with a current/active Nurs. Anes. practice Preferred Qualifications Preferred Education: Doctorate Preferred Discipline: Candidates pursuing a career in Nursing Research. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e043a062 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing CRNA Program (NO15560) Nursing CRNA Program (NO15560) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) da3669be Last Name (required) 0840940c Email (required) a7d29e74 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 3536cd66 Last Name (required) eabfadc5 Email (required) fe6475d8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
