    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/nursing-faculty-open-rank-coordinator-of-neonatal-nurse-practitioner-concentration-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "NURSING FACULTY (OPEN RANK)-COORDINATOR OF NEONATAL NURSE PRACTITIONER CONCENTRATION",
      "description": "NURSING FACULTY (OPEN RANK)-COORDINATOR OF NEONATAL NURSE PRACTITIONER CONCENTRATION - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States NURSING FACULTY (OPEN RANK)-COORDINATOR OF NEONATAL NURSE PRACTITIONER CONCENTRATION - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! NURSING FACULTY (OPEN RANK)-COORDINATOR OF NEONATAL NURSE PRACTITIONER CONCENTRATION 496551 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Nursing Add to favorites View favorites Title: NURSING FACULTY (OPEN RANK)-COORDINATOR OF NEONATAL NURSE PRACTITIONER CONCENTRATION Employee Type: Faculty Department: Family Nursing Campus Location: NURSING - ADMINISTRATION/FACUL Job Summary/Basic Functions LSU Health New Orleans School of Nursing is seeking a highly motivated individual to join our faculty as a school of nursing excellence within an academic health sciences center environment. Our nursing faculty have the opportunity to educate future nurses at the BSN, MN/MSN, PhD and DNP level, including state-of-the-art simulation laboratories; conduct nursing & interdisciplinary research; engage in faculty practice, including our nurse-run clinics; pursue entrepreneurial and consultative activities; and serve as a nursing leader and development of leadership skills through our Emergent Nurse Leader Program. We invite you to submit your curriculum vitae for the following faculty position: Coordinator of Neonatal Nurse Practitioner Concentration. Incumbent will be responsible for the academic coordination & operational management of the neonatal nurse practitioner program (“NNP”) of study to assure the quality of the educational program with primary responsibility for the development, implementation, and coordination of student didactic and clinical learning experiences; Participate in student recruitment and retention activity; Monitor student progressive statistics and program outcomes; Coordinate the development, review and revision of admissions, progression and graduation policies and procedures for the program; Serve as academic advisor and mentor students; Assist in preparation of annual reports, and any other report or correspondence required by AAC, LSBN or any other authoritative or regulatory body; Ensure NNP program remains in compliance with standards/criteria set by LSBN, NANN, NONPF, CCNE, and National Certification Corporation; Engage in professional leadership; Maintain competence in teaching, clinical practice, research, and professional service; Actively participate as a member of the School of Nursing administrative team; Collaborate with other nursing programs and professional schools to maximize educational resources & promote inter-professional collaboration; Teach NNP courses and coordinate courses; and Facilitate clinical placement of NNP Students. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: Doctorate Other Education if applicable: Research or Practice Doctorate in Nursing Required Field of Study: Nationally certified as a Neonatal Nurse Practitioner Certifications or Licenses Required: Currently licensed to practice as a Registered Nurse and Advanced Practice Registered Nurse with unencumbered Louisiana RN and APRN License (or eligible to obtain licensure in Louisiana prior to start date). Number of years required to perform the job: Five years Type of experience required to perform the job: Five Years of substantive advanced practice nursing experience with evidence of scholarship Preferred Qualifications Preferred Education: Doctorate Preferred Discipline: Candidates pursuing a career in Nursing Research. Preferred Experience: Recent clinical practice as an NNP; Prior experience in teaching at the graduate nursing level; Prior experience with graduate program administration; Prior experience guiding DNP scholarly projects or doctoral dissertations. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 290a5018 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Family Nursing (formerly: Grad (NO15530) Family Nursing (formerly: Grad (NO15530) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 2b1c4e96 Last Name (required) 92ff7cc9 Email (required) 8b0d2e0e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient