    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-lafayette-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL - Lafayette, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL - Lafayette, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL 496545 Lafayette, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - CLINICAL Employee Type: Faculty Department: Obstetrics and Gynecology Campus Location: OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is seeking a Board Certified or Board Eligible (or equivalent) OBGYN for a faculty appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track) for a position located in Lafayette, LA. Primary responsibilities include direct patient care and resident supervision in the ambulatory clinics, and operating room. In addition, a commitment to teaching residents and medical students is required. Scholarly activity involving clinical research, quality improvement projects, and other publications are strongly encouraged and expected. Responsibilities will include clinical activity, research and medical education. He/she must be board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) in Obstetrics and Gynecology and licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana before hire date. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent in Obstetrics and Gynecology; Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before start date Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert facde1a8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Obstetrics and Gynecology (NO14933) Obstetrics and Gynecology (NO14933) Locations Lafayette, Louisiana, United States Lafayette, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) e732582c Last Name (required) 495bdb82 Email (required) 75c28344 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) c1151315 Last Name (required) 41f39986 Email (required) ba04ac8a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
