    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-pediatric-cardiac-intensivist-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR, CLINICAL - PEDIATRIC CARDIAC INTENSIVIST",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR, CLINICAL - PEDIATRIC CARDIAC INTENSIVIST - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR, CLINICAL - PEDIATRIC CARDIAC INTENSIVIST - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR, CLINICAL - PEDIATRIC CARDIAC INTENSIVIST 496389 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR, CLINICAL - PEDIATRIC CARDIAC INTENSIVIST Employee Type: Faculty Department: Pediatrics Campus Location: CHILDRENS Job Summary/Basic Functions The Division of Pediatric Cardiology in the Department of Pediatrics at LSU Health Sciences Center in New Orleans are recruiting a cardiac intensivist to join a team based in the Cardiac ICU and Heart Center at Manning Family Children’s. Candidates must have an MD or DO degree (or equivalent), hold a Louisiana medical license prior to start date, and the following: • Dual boarded/eligible (or equivalent) in Pediatric Critical Care Medicine AND Pediatric Cardiology; OR Board certified/eligible (or equivalent) in Pediatric Critical Care Medicine with significant cardiac critical care experience; OR board certified/eligible (or equivalent) in Pediatric Cardiology with formal advanced training in Cardiac Intensive Care Medicine (minimum of 12 months) This is a full-time faculty position at the Assistant, Associate Professor, or Professor level (non-tenure, clinical track) with academic rank to be determined by the candidate’s credentials and experience. The faculty member will serve as attending physician responsible for the care of critically ill pediatric and adult congenital cardiac medical and surgical patients care while working collaboratively with other faculty in pediatric cardiology, cardiothoracic surgery, CICU-based advanced practice providers, and other specialists in the management of cardiac patients in the cardiac ICU as well as other locations within the health system. Clinical service time will be commensurate with the needs of the Division and intensive care unit and includes in-house night coverage. The position also entails a commitment to the teaching of physician trainees at all levels (including medical students), advanced practice providers, nurses, and other unit-based staff. Faculty members are also expected to participate in various university and hospital-driven training and educational activities, including quality improvement and care process improvement initiatives, and are strongly encouraged to pursue basic science or clinical research interests, which will require separate efforts to obtain outside grant funding wherever possible. Currently, approximately 200 heart catheterizations (75% interventional) and close to 250 cardiothoracic surgeries are performed each year at Manning Family Children’s, a 247-bed tertiary care teaching complex located in the heart of New Orleans which serves the entire State of Louisiana and the central Gulf Coast region. In late 2021, Manning Family Children’s completed a $300 million renovation, which included the creation of a state-of-the-art 28 bed CICU/Cardiac Care Unit along with expansion of the cardiac catheterization laboratories, operating rooms, pre-surgical examination rooms, PACU, surgical family facilities, and other beautiful infrastructure facilities. The CICU is staffed 24/7 with 5 cardiac intensivists and we are actively recruiting 3 more intensivists. The Heart Center participates in STS, PC4, Impact, NPC-QIC, ACTION, and other major registries. The Heart Center has an ACGME-accredited LSUHSC pediatric cardiology fellowship training program. There are excellent opportunities for clinical, translational and basic research, particularly with the LSUHSC Cardiovascular Center of Excellence as well as the Heart Center’s Research Core. The successful candidate is expected to have strong clinical skills, have an interest in research, and participate actively in the teaching of residents and fellows. Other Information About the Position Candidates must have an MD or DO degree (or equivalent), hold a Louisiana medical license prior to start date, and the following: Dual boarded/eligible (or equivalent) in Pediatric Critical Care Medicine AND Pediatric Cardiology; OR Board certified/eligible (or equivalent) in Pediatric Critical Care Medicine with significant cardiac critical care experience; OR board certified/eligible (or equivalent) in Pediatric Cardiology with formal advanced training in Cardiac Intensive Care Medicine (minimum of 12 months) Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/eligible as outlined above (see Other Information About the Position ); Licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before hire date. Preferred Qualifications Other Education if applicable: Double board eligibility or certification as outlined above Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 2c58bcb7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Pediatrics (NO14960) Pediatrics (NO14960) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 497a64a2 Last Name (required) 9b8817da Email (required) 70d585d1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Disease Group Supervisor (DGS) to be responsible for directing and managing specified Disease Groups within the LSU Cancer Center Clinical Trials Office (CC-CTO). The Disease Group Supervisor will ensure safe, compliant, efficient, and effective conduct of clinical trials within the disease groups’ portfolio. They will be expected to perform or provide guidance for direct patient care in relationship to study protocol requirements. The DGS will establish, implement, and evolve operational standards, monitor quality and progress, and supervise the CC-CTO Clinical Trial Coordinators (CTC) and RN CTC’s. Apply Now First Name (required) 317ea0e7 Last Name (required) 263769f6 Email (required) b14243c2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-research-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH 496392 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR - RESEARCH Employee Type: Faculty Department: Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence Campus Location: Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence Job Summary/Basic Functions The Cardiovascular Center of Excellence in the School of Medicine at LSU Health Sciences Center in New Orleans, LA is seeking candidates for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Candidates should have an active extramurally funded grant, the desire to participate in collaborative research projects related to cardiovascular research and teaching ability. Exceptional unfunded applicants will also be considered. Expertise in all areas of cardiovascular research will be considered, but special consideration will be given to those that complement the existing collaborative research strengths of the Center which include Heart Failure, Hypertension and Autonomic Regulation. The Cardiovascular Center of Excellence and LSUHSC-NO School of Medicine provide investigators with a scientific environment conducive to research success, with state-of-the-art Core Laboratories including Proteomics, Imaging, Cardiovascular Function, RNA and DNA Sequencing, Flow Cytometry, and Animal Care facilities. Opportunities are available for interaction with other Centers of Excellence in Neuroscience, Alcohol Research and Cancer. Anticipated duties and responsibilities will include sustaining an exceptional research program, mentoring of graduate students/post-doctoral fellows, and participating in the broad health sciences teaching activities of the Center. The institution offers competitive start-up packages and salaries. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: PhD or MD Required Field of Study: Basic Science, Health Science, or Related Field Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave; 14 paid holidays per year; and an employee health primary care clinic. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1ad0dc06 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence (NO14977) Cardiovascular Ctr Excellence (NO14977) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 54789c45 Last Name (required) 6df03789 Email (required) a42728a9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you PROCUREMENT ANALYST 1, 2 or 3 Purchasing (NO16630) LSU Health New Orleans Division of Purchasing is seeking motivated individuals for the title of Procurement Analyst 1, 2 or 3. PROGRAM MANAGER Med-Allergy and Clinical Immun (NO14921) The department of Community Population Medicine is seeking a PROGRAM MANAGER. The incumbent will provide outreach, research, and evaluation capacity for programs managed by the Face the Fight program in the Division of Community and Population Medicine. DISEASE GROUP SUPERVISOR Center of excellence-Cancer (NO14974) The LSU Cancer Center is seeking a Di