    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-clinical-pulmonary-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY 497492 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/ ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, PULMONARY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Med-Pulmonary/Critical Care Me Campus Location: MEDICINE/NEW ORLEANS Job Summary/Basic Functions The LSU Health Sciences Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Pulmonary and Critical Care in New Orleans, seeks a board certified / board eligible physician in Pulmonary Disease and Critical Care Medicine to join our faculty at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (non-tenure, clinical track). This faculty member will practice at University Medical Center – New Orleans (UMCNO) and will work in the ICU as well as the outpatient pulmonary clinic. Work as an inpatient pulmonary consultant is also possible. In all care areas, the successful candidate will maintain excellence in patient care, teaching, and research integrity. Academic appointment will be commensurate with professional achievement. Current trainees or junior faculty with an excellent track record of inpatient and outpatient care proficiency are strongly encouraged to apply. Our group thrives on collaboration and looks forward to adding another team-oriented faculty member to our outstanding academic faculty group practice. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Certifications or Licenses Required: ABIM board eligible/certified (or equivalent) in Pulmonary and/or Critical Care; licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities prior to start date. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Experience: Pulmonary/Critical Care fellowship with interest in CVS/ICU Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave, and14 paid holidays per year. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e8aedb51 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Med-Nephrology (NO14924) Med-Nephrology (NO14924) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 70b5fd0a Last Name (required) 2bb1a6ad Email (required) 6f53b0c9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you OMFS SURGERY COORDINATOR LSUNO Oral Surgery (NO12260) LSU Health New Orleans, School of Dentistry, Department of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery is seeking an organized and patient-focused OMFS Surgery Coordinator. IT HELP DESK BACKUP ANALYST 1 - 4 Information Technology-Adminis (NO16730) LSU Health New Orleans is seeking candidates for an IT HELP DESK BACKUP ANALYST 1 - 4. DEPARTMENT COORDINATOR Medical Laboratory Science (NO10515) The Medical Laboratory Science department is seeking a DEPARTMENT COORDINATOR. The Department Coordinator serves as the primary administrative and operational support professional for the Department of Medical Laboratory Science in the LSU Health Sciences Center New Orleans School of Health Professions. Apply Now First Name (required) 31e1296a Last Name (required) 1619940c Email (required) 1d3c823c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
