    "https://careers.lsuhsc.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-professor-clinical-neonatology-new-orleans-louisiana-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, NEONATOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, NEONATOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, NEONATOLOGY - New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR - CLINICAL, NEONATOLOGY 497505 New Orleans, Louisiana, United States Faculty Medicine Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR / ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR / PROFESSOR- CLINICAL, NEONATOLOGY Employee Type: Faculty Department: Pediatrics Campus Location: CHILDRENS Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Pediatrics, Division of Neonatology at Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center School of Medicine in New Orleans, is seeking an academic Neonatologist to join our 16-member faculty group. The Division of Neonatology provides inpatient care for sick infants at Manning Family Children’s and six other community hospitals in the region. We are involved in the education of the largest group of medical students, pediatric residents, and neonatology fellows in the state. The Department of Pediatrics at LSU Health Sciences Center New Orleans is dedicated to excellence in patient care, mastery in teaching and continuous learning. The Department boasts approximately eighty faculty members representing all pediatric sub-specialties. Training programs include an annual medical school class of two hundred students and approximately one hundred post-graduate trainees in categorical pediatrics, medicine-pediatrics, child neurology, combined pediatrics and emergency medicine and most pediatric sub-specialty fellowship areas. Academic appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor (non-tenure, clinical track), with rank to be determined by the candidate’s credentials and experience. The successful candidate will participate in a broad range of activities. Primary clinical responsibilities of the position include patient care in a variety of settings. Educational responsibilities include supervision and instruction of medical students, residents, fellows and other learners from the multi-disciplinary LSUHSC community. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the advancement of scholarly or educational activities within the department. There are abundant opportunities for educational, clinical, translational, and quality and outcomes research initiatives across the Health Sciences Center. Other Information About the Position Manning Family Children’s is Louisiana’s largest free-standing children’s hospital and serves as the primary pediatric teaching site for LSUHSC Pediatrics. Manning Family Children’s is a 263-bed, not-for-profit pediatric medical center offering a comprehensive range of services for children from birth to 21 years, with more than 600 pediatric providers and 3,000 employees solely dedicated to the care of kids. With an unwavering commitment to child health, we have proudly served as the Gulf South’s only comprehensive children’s hospital for 70 years – transforming countless lives since we first opened our doors in 1955. The hospital is home to a growing array of pediatric subspecialists and houses state-of-the-art facilities. Minimum Qualifications Required Education: MD or equivalent Other Education if applicable: Fellowship in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine Certifications or Licenses Required: Board certified/board eligible (or equivalent) in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine; licensed to practice medicine in Louisiana and credentialed with all required entities before start date. Additional Information About Our School/Department Comprehensive benefits are available to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement plans; generous annual and sick leave, and14 paid holidays per year. See following link for more details on our benefits offerings: LSUHSC, New Orleans - Benefits Other employee benefits include a full-service credit union, wellness benefits featuring complimentary fitness center membership for employees and their spouses, employee assistance program, campus assistance program, and pet insurance option. More information about these benefits can be found on this webpage: Additional Benefits Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 4bc89df4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Pediatrics (NO14960) Pediatrics (NO14960) Locations New Orleans, Louisiana, United States New Orleans, Louisiana, United States First Name (required) 3c9edd83 Last Name (required) 15ddc14e Email (required) 0eba910b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you OMFS SURGERY COORDINATOR LSUNO Oral Surgery (NO12260) LSU Health New Orleans, School of Dentistry, Department of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery is seeking an organized and patient-focused OMFS Surgery Coordinator. IT HELP DESK BACKUP ANALYST 1 - 4 Information Technology-Adminis (NO16730) LSU Health New Orleans is seeking candidates for an IT HELP DESK BACKUP ANALYST 1 - 4. DEPARTMENT COORDINATOR Medical Laboratory Science (NO10515) The Medical Laboratory Science department is seeking a DEPARTMENT COORDINATOR. The Department Coordinator serves as the primary administrative and operational support professional for the Department of Medical Laboratory Science in the LSU Health Sciences Center New Orleans School of Health Professions. Apply Now First Name (required) 14dd517b Last Name (required) c826fb34 Email (required) a9ec5d42 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
